{"id": "EUVD-2026-10575", "enisaUuid": "01fffda9-565e-3a9a-8ba0-e2de075dc82e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntls: Fix race condition in tls_sw_cancel_work_tx()\n\nThis issue was discovered during a code audit.\n\nAfter cancel_delayed_work_sync() is called from tls_sk_proto_close(),\ntx_work_handler() can still be scheduled from paths such as the\nDelayed ACK handler or ksoftirqd.\nAs a result, the tx_work_handler() worker may dereference a freed\nTLS object.\n\nThe following is a simple race scenario:\n\n          cpu0                         cpu1\n\ntls_sk_proto_close()\n  tls_sw_cancel_work_tx()\n                                 tls_write_space()\n                                   tls_sw_write_space()\n                                     if (!test_and_set_bit(BIT_TX_SCHEDULED, &tx_ctx->tx_bitmask))\n    set_bit(BIT_TX_SCHEDULED, &ctx->tx_bitmask);\n    cancel_delayed_work_sync(&ctx->tx_work.work);\n                                     schedule_delayed_work(&tx_ctx->tx_work.work, 0);\n\nTo prevent this race condition, cancel_delayed_work_sync() is\nreplaced with disable_delayed_work_sync().", "datePublished": "2026-03-10T17:28:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:35:39", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5de36d6cee74a92c1a21b260bc507e64bc451de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/854cd32bc74fe573353095e90958490e4e4d641b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17153f154f80be2b47ebf52840f2d8f724eb2f3b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bb09315f93dce6acc54bf59e5a95ba7365c2be4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23240", "GHSA-c96v-vvf3-2p7r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1002e312-900d-311d-8aa9-f12b36d58e4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "35b66f9c-0004-3bf1-ab2a-58f2bb2ffc95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.75"}, {"id": "438bc505-f9d8-3274-8a18-d7f5f72c30fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f87e62d45e51b12d48d2cb46b5cde8f83b866bc4 <a5de36d6cee74a92c1a21b260bc507e64bc451de"}, {"id": "564d1ec2-a1fe-370a-828a-98a373a089e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "78339aae-5833-3208-9d67-16d5af6c8add", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f87e62d45e51b12d48d2cb46b5cde8f83b866bc4 <7bb09315f93dce6acc54bf59e5a95ba7365c2be4"}, {"id": "87794b79-6f6a-3838-9fb6-86205173d949", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.16"}, {"id": "8bf090e1-51bf-36a6-98d2-c63f753beb06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f87e62d45e51b12d48d2cb46b5cde8f83b866bc4 <17153f154f80be2b47ebf52840f2d8f724eb2f3b"}, {"id": "8eb1a693-ea23-30c2-8c80-e03e87f1963d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f87e62d45e51b12d48d2cb46b5cde8f83b866bc4 <854cd32bc74fe573353095e90958490e4e4d641b"}, {"id": "b2741c63-f59e-3d47-88e0-b19258139efc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "d5fa8b3b-8a1b-38aa-974d-0789d3bed92f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0af10235-a60a-35b1-a5dc-71197e432079", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}